  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "comment": "The embedding models the embedder image bakes in. Since DECISIONS 140 (2026-11-12) the Team record (`record`) and the lessons (`lesson`) use the SAME model, bge-small-en-v1.5 (384-d): the two names stay so the request format does not change, and an entry that is identical to an earlier one is exported once (the image holds one copy; the later name is a link to it). Revisions are Hugging Face commit hashes; every source file is checked against its sha256 at image build time. The model ships in fp32 (no quantization). `toolchain` is the export tool versions (the hashed lock files requirements-build.lock and requirements-runtime.lock pin the same versions) and `outputs` the sha256 of every file the export writes; both are part of the spec, so a different tool version or a different output is a different spec. `referenceFiles` are the extra files of the reference snapshot the parity check compares against. Changing a revision, a tool version, the pooling, the truncation or the wrapper tokens changes the vectors: spec is a hash of those (embedder_core.spec_id), the broker pins the same value in packages/cloud-contracts/src/team-record-storage.ts, and a different spec means a new vector index and a full re-embed. To record new outputs run tools/export_models.py with --update-lock.",
